==================================================
  TASK 3.1 – NO TRANSACTION (partial-state failure)
==================================================

BEFORE  → stock: 5, sold: 0, orders: 0

Running checkout WITHOUT a transaction, forcing the order step to crash...
✖ Checkout threw: SIMULATED CRASH: order persistence failed after payment + inventory update

--------------------------------------------------
  DATABASE STATE AFTER THE FAILURE
--------------------------------------------------
Payment charged        : YES (customer billed)
Stock before / after   : 5 → 4  (decremented)
Sold before / after    : 0 → 1
Orders before / after  : 0 → 0  (NO order created)
--------------------------------------------------

❌ INCONSISTENT STATE — payment taken & stock reduced, but NO order exists.
   This is exactly what transactions must prevent.


[2m   step 2 / 2[0m

[34m── [1mAFTER — Transaction: rollback on failure + concurrent consistency[0m[34m ───[0m

==================================================
  TASK 3.2/3.3 – MONGODB TRANSACTIONS
==================================================

--- Part A: Atomic rollback on a forced failure ---

BEFORE → stock: 5, orders: 0
✖ Checkout threw (expected): SIMULATED CRASH: order persistence failed after payment + inventory update
AFTER  → stock: 5, orders: 0
✅ ROLLED BACK — stock unchanged, no order. No partial state.

--- Part B: Concurrent transactional checkouts ---

Stock = 5; firing 15 concurrent transactional checkouts (qty 1)...

--------------------------------------------------
  CONCURRENT RESULT
--------------------------------------------------
Initial stock          : 5
Concurrent checkouts   : 15
Committed (orders)     : 5
Rejected (stock/conflict): 10
Final stock            : 0   (never < 0)
Orders created         : 5
Units sold (sold field): 5
--------------------------------------------------

✅ CONSISTENT — orders created == stock consumed == sold; no oversell, no partial updates.


